Package: diplomacyR
Title: Play, Simulate, and Analyse the Board Game Diplomacy
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: A complete engine for the strategic board game Diplomacy, covering
    the standard seven-power pre-1914 European map. Provides a rules-accurate
    simultaneous-movement adjudicator (hold, move, support, convoy, retreat, and
    build phases) validated against the Diplomacy Adjudicator Test Cases, a set
    of scriptable bots for automated play, batch simulation with outcome
    analysis, and a comprehensive 'shiny' application for interactive play and
    exploration. Board states and analyses render as 'ggplot2' objects.
